From 73df95dfafe91fbebad80f17f4c6ace173789445 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:20:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] vulkan/wsi: pass libbe on to the driver that links the
 WSI

The first build of the renga-26.3 branch on Renga (GCC 15.3) compiled
all of NVK and then failed to link libvulkan_nouveau.so:

  wsi_common_renga.cpp:370: undefined reference to `BBitmap::ColorSpace() const'
  wsi_common_renga.cpp:288: undefined reference to `BScreen::BScreen(screen_id)'
  ... be_app, B_MAIN_SCREEN_ID, BScreen::WaitForRetrace ...

wsi_common_renga.cpp uses the Interface Kit, and meson.build adds
cpp.find_library('be') to platform_deps, but platform_deps is only a
dependency of the libvulkan_wsi static library. The driver pulls that
library in through idep_vulkan_wsi with link_whole, and -lbe did not
appear on its link line. Add platform_deps to idep_vulkan_wsi's
dependencies so every driver that links the WSI also links its
platform libraries.

On other platforms platform_deps is empty or holds only DirectX headers
(Windows), so nothing changes there.

Not yet built on Renga.

Generated-by: LLM
Biblioklept: this commit message was written by an AI model.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVRp8mDpV9jS7UpPk2uhfF
(cherry picked from commit 423ba7c0ec99c1b39fb8866e3db71a17b6865b27)
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build b/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
index bc23ebe..617db1e 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
@@ -87,8 +87,11 @@ else
     # Instruct users of this library to link with --whole-archive.  Otherwise,
     # our weak function overloads may not resolve properly.
     link_whole : libvulkan_wsi,
+    # platform_deps too: libbe for the Renga WSI. As a dependency of the
+    # static library only, -lbe did not reach the driver's link line and
+    # libvulkan_nouveau.so failed with undefined BBitmap/BScreen symbols.
     dependencies : [
-      idep_vulkan_wsi_headers, dep_libudev
+      idep_vulkan_wsi_headers, dep_libudev, platform_deps
     ]
   )
 endif
-- 
2.43.0


From 26a2a56a32a99d98e3905b11cc3784f547ebdde6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:27:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] util: link libgnu for inotify on Renga

fossilize_db.c uses inotify_init1(), inotify_add_watch() and
inotify_rm_watch() when the top-level meson.build finds sys/inotify.h.
Renga ships that header (headers/compatibility/gnu/sys/inotify.h) and
implements the functions in libgnu (src/libs/gnu/inotify.cpp), not in
libroot, and nothing in Mesa linked libgnu.

NVK linked anyway because rustc's Haiku target adds -lbsd -lroot
-lnetwork -lgnu to every link that includes Rust code. A driver without
Rust code fails: the Zink build on Renga 143b8c30, from the same util
sources, stopped at

  fossilize_db.c:467: undefined reference to `inotify_init1'

Add libgnu to libmesa_util's dependencies on Haiku/Renga whenever
sys/inotify.h is present, so the dependency is stated rather than
inherited from Rust.

Not yet built on Renga.

Generated-by: LLM
Biblioklept: this commit message was written by an AI model.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVRp8mDpV9jS7UpPk2uhfF
(cherry picked from commit 32e1fb32c5ae1014925a2d359adce74b37d4a6ef)
---
 src/util/meson.build | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util/meson.build b/src/util/meson.build
index 72d8660..64d9d0e 100644
--- a/src/util/meson.build
+++ b/src/util/meson.build
@@ -336,6 +336,13 @@ if with_platform_haiku
   deps_for_libmesa_util += dep_network
 endif
 
+# Renga provides inotify, which fossilize_db.c uses when sys/inotify.h is
+# found, in libgnu rather than libroot. Link it explicitly: NVK only linked
+# so far because the Rust standard library happens to add -lgnu.
+if host_machine.system() == 'haiku' and cc.check_header('sys/inotify.h')
+  deps_for_libmesa_util += cc.find_library('gnu')
+endif
+
 if with_perfetto
   files_mesa_util += files(
     'perf/u_perfetto.cc',
-- 
2.43.0


From 8af33bcab554bc18c6e932d142a71f18c15a7657 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: X512 <danger_mail@list.ru>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:28:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] zink: Haiku support (X512's haiku-zink, adapted to Mesa
 26.3)

X512's "zink: Haiku support" (549fbf65) and "hgl: drop dead code"
(b7b399ff) from X547/mesa haiku-zink, a Mesa 25.1-devel tree, carried to
26.3 so that Renga's OpenGL (Zink on NVK) builds from the same Mesa as
NVK instead of from a second, older tree.

What the change does:

- EGL on Haiku creates a Zink screen instead of a software one.
- The hgl frontend gives Zink window drawables through kopper, as a
  headless VkSurface plus the window's BitmapHook (the RengaWsi /
  VideoStreams surface ABI, zink_kopper_haiku.cpp).
- Kopper gets a KOPPER_HAIKU display-target type, keyed by the
  BitmapHook.
- kopper_loader_info gains bitmapHook.

Changes from the original while carrying it:

- kopper_interface.h moved to src/gallium/include; bitmapHook is added
  there.
- The kopper hunks are re-applied by hand against 26.3, which spells
  unreachable() as UNREACHABLE(). Two switches (swapchain sizing, dts
  table init) already list KOPPER_HAIKU in 26.3.
- Dropped as unneeded on 26.3:
  - the renderdoc_app.h hunk, which is upstream now;
  - the libsync.h "#error" and the include guards around it in
    egl_dri2.c and drisw.c (neither file is built for Haiku);
  - the inline_sw_helper.h include, since egl_haiku.cpp includes
    zink_public.h itself;
  - whitespace-only hunks in zink_screen.c.
- egl_haiku.cpp calls zink_create_screen() directly instead of keeping
  the software path behind "#if 0", and fails eglInitialize cleanly
  (EGL_NOT_INITIALIZED, winsys freed) when no Zink screen can be made,
  instead of building a display on a NULL screen.

Checked: tools/crosscheck/mesa.sh (clang -fsyntax-only for
x86_64-unknown-haiku against Renga a1a83da2 headers) passes for all 23
Zink sources, hgl.c and egl_haiku.cpp. Not built with GCC or run.

Generated-by: LLM
